From: Rainist7heta <thetamkz621@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:44:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soxr: derive the OpenMP runtime in soxr.pc from CMake

libsoxr is built as a static library with -DWITH_OPENMP=ON, but soxr.pc.in
has no Libs.private entry. The stage appends a hard-coded "-lgomp" after
installation, which is only correct when the objects were compiled by GCC
(GOMP ABI). clang lowers OpenMP to the kmp ABI and needs libomp, so a
clang-built libsoxr fails to link with -lgomp.

Let CMake decide: FindOpenMP records the runtime it used in OpenMP_C_LIB_NAMES
and where it found it in OpenMP_C_LIBRARIES; put both into the template and
drop the hard-coded value. The names alone are not enough: FindOpenMP decides
"found" by compiling and linking through the compiler driver with -fopenmp,
and the driver appends its own -L. A distribution can therefore report OpenMP
found while a bare -lomp does not resolve (Debian keeps libomp.so in
/usr/lib/llvm-19/lib, outside the linker's default search path), so emit the
-L entries too, ahead of the -l ones. The .pc is only consumed on the build
host, and it is not part of the packaged artifact.

When OpenMP was not found both parts stay empty, matching the serial objects.

---
 CMakeLists.txt | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/soxr.pc.in |  1 +
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index ee48f6c..35fe5cc 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -109,6 +109,30 @@ if (WITH_OPENMP)
   if (OPENMP_FOUND)
     set (CMAKE_C_FLAGS "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS} ${OpenMP_C_FLAGS}")
     set (CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} ${OpenMP_CXX_FLAGS}")
+    # pkg-config consumers of a *static* libsoxr must be told which OpenMP
+    # runtime the objects were compiled against, and where that runtime lives.
+    # Do not hard-code -lgomp: clang lowers OpenMP to the kmp ABI, whose
+    # runtime is libomp, and some distributions keep libomp.so outside the
+    # linker's default search path, so the name alone is not enough.
+    if (OpenMP_C_FOUND)
+      foreach (_soxr_omp_lib ${OpenMP_C_LIBRARIES})
+        if (IS_ABSOLUTE "${_soxr_omp_lib}")
+          get_filename_component (_soxr_omp_dir "${_soxr_omp_lib}" DIRECTORY)
+          list (APPEND _soxr_omp_dirs "${_soxr_omp_dir}")
+        endif()
+      endforeach()
+      if (_soxr_omp_dirs)
+        list (REMOVE_DUPLICATES _soxr_omp_dirs)
+        foreach (_soxr_omp_dir ${_soxr_omp_dirs})
+          string (APPEND SOXR_PC_PRIVATE " -L${_soxr_omp_dir}")
+        endforeach()
+      endif()
+      foreach (_soxr_omp ${OpenMP_C_LIB_NAMES})
+        if (NOT _soxr_omp STREQUAL "pthread")
+          string (APPEND SOXR_PC_PRIVATE " -l${_soxr_omp}")
+        endif()
+      endforeach()
+    endif()
     if (MINGW) # Is this still needed?
       set (CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS "${CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS} ${OpenMP_C_FLAGS}")
       set (CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS "${CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS} ${OpenMP_C_FLAGS}")
diff --git a/src/soxr.pc.in b/src/soxr.pc.in
index 69d225b..e86bac0 100644
--- a/src/soxr.pc.in
+++ b/src/soxr.pc.in
@@ -2,4 +2,5 @@ Name: ${PROJECT_NAME}
 Description: ${DESCRIPTION_SUMMARY}
 Version: ${PROJECT_VERSION}
 Libs: -L${LIB_INSTALL_DIR} -l${PROJECT_NAME}
+Libs.private:@SOXR_PC_PRIVATE@
 Cflags: -I${INCLUDE_INSTALL_DIR}
